## 3.9 Determination of MUC1 in human serum
As another considerable performance of biosensor, the practicality was investigated by recovery assay based on standard addition method. Briefly, the human serum was diluted 40 times with PBS \((\mathrm{pH}=7.4)\) and then used for preparation of different concentrations of MUC1. Then, the biosensors incubated with different concentrations of MUC1 were detected by the ECL signals, and the found concentrations were calculated according to the linear equation. As shown in Table 3, the recoveries varied from \(97.3\%\) to \(100.7\%\), showing that the developed biosensor held remarkable application potential in clinical diagnosis and treatment.
