## Highlights
Restriction of intramolecular motions (RIM) by metal-organic frameworks for electrochemiluminescence enhancement: 2D \(\mathbf{Zr}_{12}\)-adb nanoplate as a novel ECL tag for the construction of biosensing platform
- A new and efficient strategy was proposed for the first time to enhance ECL, named RIM by MOFs for ECL enhancement.
- \(\mathrm{Zr}_{12}\)-adb nanoplates was synthesized as a bright ECL emitter to construct highly sensitive and selective ECL biosensors.
- The developed ECL biosensor realized ultrasensitive detection for MUC1.
